This loop is basically a duplication of the code just below with only the specificity of handling the wheel:
```c++
        if (mi->Wheel && mi->Wheel == mj->Wheel)
          a[i*n+j] += mi->WheelCoeff * mj->WheelCoeff * mi->Wheel->InvInertia;
```
Since this code is guarded by the `if (mi->Wheel)` it can be integrated in the legacy code rather than duplicating the loops.

This code should be moved before the calls to `Constrain`:
```c++
    LMultiplier[ftRoll].value = Constrain(LMultiplier[ftRoll].Min, LMultiplier[ftRoll].value, LMultiplier[ftRoll].Max);
    LMultiplier[ftSide].value = Constrain(LMultiplier[ftSide].Min, LMultiplier[ftSide].value, LMultiplier[ftSide].Max);
```
The reason being that once the update of `LMultiplier[ftRoll].Max` will be moved to `ConfigureWheelSpinRows`, `Constrain` shall be called **after** `LMultiplier[ftRoll].Max` has been updated.
